        "## 15.19 Encoder-only, decoder-only, and encoder-decoder models\n",
        "\n",
        "The three main Transformer families differ in their attention pattern and task objective.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Architecture | Attention pattern | Main output | Typical tasks |\n",
        "|---|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Encoder-only | bidirectional self-attention | contextual input representation | classification, retrieval, tagging |\n",
        "| Decoder-only | causal self-attention | next-token distribution | generation, completion, chat |\n",
        "| Encoder-decoder | source encoder plus target decoder cross-attention | conditional target distribution | translation, summarization |\n",
        "\n",
        "Mathematically, encoder-only models estimate representations useful for conditional predictions such as\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(y\\mid x_1,\\ldots,x_T).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Decoder-only models estimate left-to-right conditional distributions such as\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(w_{t+1}\\mid w_1,\\ldots,w_t).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Encoder-decoder models estimate conditional sequence distributions such as\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "P(y_1,\\ldots,y_m\\mid x_1,\\ldots,x_T)\n",
        "=\\prod_{t=1}^m P(y_t\\mid y_1,\\ldots,y_{t-1},x_1,\\ldots,x_T).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "## 15.20 Mathematical comparison with RNNs\n",
        "\n",
        "An RNN computes hidden states recursively:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "h_t=f(h_{t-1},x_t).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus information from token $j$ reaches token $i$ through a chain of intermediate states.  A Transformer computes direct token-token scores:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "s_{ij}=q_i^Tk_j/\\sqrt{d_k}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus token $i$ can attend directly to token $j$ in one layer.  This shorter interaction path is one reason Transformers can model long-range dependencies effectively.\n",
        "\n",
        "However, the direct interaction comes with quadratic cost in $T$.  The mathematical tradeoff is:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{recurrence path length }O(T)\\quad\\text{versus}\\quad\\text{attention score matrix size }O(T^2).\n",
        "$$\n",
